---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — The Daily AI Pulse"
  description="How this static publication handles reader data."
>
  <article class="information-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">READER INFORMATION</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This site is a static publication hosted on GitHub Pages. It has no reader accounts or email
      signup form.
    </p>
    <section>
      <h2>Reading and searching</h2>
      <p>
        Stories are delivered as static pages. Search uses a generated index in your browser; the
        publication does not run its own search server. The current site code does not include a
        publication analytics tracker.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        GitHub says that visiting a GitHub Pages site causes the visitor’s IP address to be logged
        for security purposes. See{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection">
          GitHub Pages data collection
        </a>{' '}
        and{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement">
          GitHub’s privacy statement
        </a>{' '}
        for its practices.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Following a source link, the RSS feed in a third-party reader, or a GitHub issue takes you
        to services with their own privacy practices. If email subscriptions are added, this page
        will need an update before addresses are collected.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
